# s3-12: dual-path DesktopHostBackend and desktop.computerBackend

## mixdog-tools/src/desktop/mod.rs
After the line `mod computer_command;` add:
pub mod computer_desktop_host;

## mixdog-core-config/src/config/mod.rs  (not a hot file; one owner-less re-export block, apply with this wave)
After the line `pub use desktop::SessionRetention;` add:
pub use desktop::ComputerBackendChoice;
After the line `pub use desktop::browser_cookie_auto_import;` add:
pub use desktop::computer_backend;

## Cargo
No new dependency edge, workspace member or lockfile entry: the file uses only crates mixdog-tools already depends on.

## Compose / service registration
None here. s3-19 (compose_computer) selects the backend:
  if mixdog_core_config::config::computer_backend(&config) == mixdog_core_config::config::ComputerBackendChoice::DesktopHost
      => Arc::new(DesktopHostBackend::new(host_channel, blobs, session_id, observe_only))
  where `blobs: Arc<dyn ComputerBlobs>` is implemented over the core blob store, and the section reports
  `DesktopHostBackend::backend_name()` ("desktopHost") as ComputerSection.backend.
  The wrapper GatedComputerBackend goes around it as around the helper backend.
  Session lifecycle: `DesktopHostBackend::session_control("execution_end" | "session_release" | "turn_settle", extra, timeout)`
  is the client's sendComputerSessionControl for the turn settlement and the idle release of the session.
  Not in this backend, left to the selecting pool (review s3-12): the client's per-session bookkeeping around those
  controls (execution_end only for a session with an active execution, the 2-minute deferred release and its hold while a
  command runs, new input refused until a pending release is confirmed, release of every host-bound session at shutdown),
  the saved-login fill's turn_id/runtime_id and owner attachment, and computerSecretBind/computerSecretInput
  (ComputerSecretHost) over host/computer/command.

## SERVICE_PENDING (compose_flip.rs)
No name is removed: host/computer/command is a core -> host request, not a protocol method the core serves.
